      "writtenOn": "2026-02-02T14:29:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That won\u0027t work, Most of IOMMU infrastructure and IOMMU drivers are abstracted from the host/guest, so they create requests with `REQ_MEM_DEST_HYP_IOMMU` for both host and guest.\n\nSo the allocation of the request will differ but the content is the same. I suggest we keep one IOMMU type and based on the location (smccc ret or vcpu-\u003ereq) the kernel devices how to top up the IOMMU pool.\n\nI see already vcpu can be NULL in `handle_hyp_req()`",
      "range": {
