      "message": "Ha you\u0027re right, it should be\n\n```\nif {\n    req \u003d pkvm_hyp_req_reserve(hyp_vcpu, KVM_HYP_REQ_TYPE_MEM);\n    if (WARN_ON(!req))\n        return NULL;\n        \n    req-\u003ememcache.dest \u003d REQ_MEM_DEST_HYP_IOMMU;\n    req-\u003ememcache.nr_pages \u003d 1;\n    req-\u003ememcache.sz_alloc \u003d size;\n\n} else {\n    req-\u003etype \u003d KVM_HYP_REQ_TYPE_MEM_IOMMU\n    req-\u003emem.nr_pages \u003d 1 \u003c\u003c order;\n}\n```\n\nAnd in the hyp_vcpu block I should of course also set the type to KVM_HYP_REQ_TYPE_MEM_IOMMU.",
